{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/156950-bound-ghosts-interaction-gmc-edition","id":156950,"title":"Bound-Ghosts Interaction, GMC edition.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-02T15:46:08-07:00","id":156950,"title":"Bound-Ghosts Interaction, GMC edition.","content":"These rules replace the rules for reinforcing Ghosts with Plasm; for the purposes of these rules, Ghosts have Thresholds just like Geists and Bound do.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost Feeding:</b> A Bound who is interacting with a Ghost may Reflexively spend 1 Plasm to imbue the Ghost with a trace of their deathly solidity. A Ghost that has been &quot;fed&quot; is shocked into consciousness for a Scene; a fed Ghost's Integrity may be increased or lowered as if they were alive.<br /> <br /> More interestingly, a Rank 1 Ghost that is &quot;fed&quot; becomes as fully conscious as a Rank 2 Ghost for that Scene, before their memories fade away again; additionally, a Ghost regains Essence equal to half the Sin-Eater's Psyche.<br /> <br /> <b>Honorary Rank:</b> A Bound's Keystone is a marker of their authority; as long as their Keystone is &quot;in hand&quot;, they are considered to have an Honorary Rank of 3 whenever they interact with Ghosts; they may spend 2 Plasm and 1 WP to increase their Honorary Rank to 4 for a scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Summoning, Exorcism, Abjuration, Binding, and Warding:</b> The Bound have a certain amount of... supernatural influence over Ghosts. If the Ghost's Threshold matches that of a Bound or their Geist, they may apply the +3 bonus from their Keystone to any attempt to Summon, Exorcise, Abjure, Bind, or Ward against Ghosts.<br /> <br /> Additionally, Sin-Eaters benefit from the following option:<ul><li><b>Cena de los Muertes:</b> The Bound may spend 1 Plasm as part of any attempt to Summon or Bind a Ghost; doing so &quot;feeds&quot; any Ghost that is summoned or bound.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Skeleton Keys:</b> The Bound may &quot;unlock&quot; a Ghost as if they were a Manifestation; doing so grants the Ghost the benefits of Caul \u2022 for that Key, as if the Bound had rolled a single success on the activation roll. They may spend up to 5 Plasm on this option; each point after the first either increases the Caul rating (to a maximum of Caul \u2022\u2022\u2022 or the Ghost's Rank, whichever is lower), or increase the Activation successes by 1.<br /> <br /> Ghosts treat their Rank as 1 higher if the Key falls under their Threshold.<br /> <br /> There are rumors that certain other Manifestations may be emulated in this way; that haunted houses can be built through Boneyard Ghosts, or that Poltergeists can be armed through Rage.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">OK, so Skeleton Keys is kinda out of nowhere; I just kinda thought it was appropriate. I'm probably wrong in finding it appropriate.<br /> <br /> But come on, it's at least <i>cool.</i></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}